[ti:Day 10]

[00:00.00]compulsory [kəmˈpʌlsəri]a. 强制的；义务的 例 The dispute was settled by compulsory arbitration. 搭 be compulsory for 对…是强制的 / compulsory education 义务教育
[00:14.76]attrition [əˈtrɪʃn]n. 磨损；产品耗损；(退休等造成的)人员 自然缩减 例 It is more a strategy of preventing attrition to other carriers, companies or sites than it is about true customer satisfaction.
[00:32.88]specimen [ˈspesɪmən]n. 样本；标本；样品
[00:36.36]boredom [ˈbɔːdəm]n. 厌烦，厌倦；无聊 例 He had given up practising swimming out of sheer boredom. 搭 avoid boredom 消愁解闷 / group boredom 群体无聊
[00:49.44]histogram [ˈhɪstəɡræm]n. 柱状图，直方图 例 You can show the research project as a report or a histogram.
[00:59.16]joint [dʒɔɪnt]a. 联合的，共同的；合办的；共有的； 连带的 例 The joint venture is integrated into the dominant parent's management system. 搭 joint responsibility 连带责任
[01:14.28]redouble [ˌriːˈdʌbl]vt. 再加倍；(使)翻两番 例 We should redouble efforts to adjust the economic structure.
[01:24.48]caliber [ˈkælɪbə(r)]n. 水准；能力，素质；口径；枪弹的 直径 例 The members of a once-outstanding economics team have left and have not been replaced by experts of like calibre. 搭 caliber ruler 卡尺
[01:42.36]dexterity [dekˈsterəti]n. 灵巧；熟练；敏捷 例 The new assistant handled the problem with dexterity.
[01:51.84]inward [ˈɪnwəd]a. 输入的；进口的；内部的；国内的 例 In the face of threats from abroad, it can be tempting to seek comfort by turning inward.
[02:04.44]recompense [ˈrekəmpens]n. 补偿；赔偿；报酬；酬金 vt. 酬 谢；偿还 例 Our company will recompense your friend for extra work. 搭 recompense sb. for sth. 因某事酬谢或报答某 人
[02:19.08]abrasion [əˈbreɪʒn]n. 摩擦；磨耗；磨损处；(皮肤等的)擦 伤处 例 Abrasion tests are generally carried out before the market entry of the new products.
[02:32.52]standing [ˈstændɪŋ]a. 停滞的；常设的；长期存在的 n. 站 立；身份；声望
[02:37.68]outweigh [ˌaʊtˈweɪ]vt. 重量上(或价值上)超过 例 Technical innovation will increase production costs, but the gains are expected to outweigh the financial outlays.
[02:53.52]identify [aɪˈdentɪfaɪ]vt. 认出；鉴定；识别；使等同于 vi. 认同；确定 例 Because the system cannot identify these users, it serves the same page to all of them. 搭 identify with 认同
[03:09.48]overestimate [ˌəʊvərˈestɪmeɪt]vt. 高估；对…评价过高 [ˌəʊvərˈestɪmət]n. 过高的估计；过高的评价 例 We always overestimate what we can achieve in a day while underestimating what we can achieve in a year.
[03:28.32]cartridge [ˈkɑːtrɪdʒ]n. (打印机的)墨盒；夹头；录音带盒； 编码磁带 例 You can get up to 27 percent more pages per ink cartridge in this way.
[03:40.32]swing [swɪŋ]n. 摇摆；涨落；波动 搭 in full swing 正在全力进行中；正处于全盛时 期 invisible assets 无形资产；账外资产 overtime allowance 加班补助；加班费
[03:51.96]recruiter [rɪˈkruːtə(r)]n. 征兵人员；招聘人员
[03:56.04]meritocracy [ˌmerɪˈtɒkrəsi]n. 精英；英才管理(制度)；英才管 理的社会 搭 academic meritocracy 学术精英管理
[04:04.80]architect [ˈɑːkɪtekt]n. 建筑师；(某一专门领域的)设计师， 创造者 例 Deng Xiaoping is believed to be China's chief architect of economic reform.
[04:17.64]draft [drɑːft]n. 汇票；付款通知 例 I enclose here with a draft the sum of 100 dollars.
[04:25.32]aggrieve [əˈɡriːv]vt. 使悲痛；使委屈；侵害 例 Personal privacy is aggrieved due to imperfection of network management system.
[04:37.32]blueprint [ˈbluːprɪnt]n. 蓝图
[04:40.32]contradict [ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt]v. 反驳；同…矛盾，同…抵触 例 Local policy may contradict this execution style for the pattern. 搭 contradict oneself 自相矛盾
[04:54.36]punctuality [ˌpʌŋktʃuˈæləti]n. 准时 例 Punctuality plays an important role in formal business negotiations.
[05:05.40]turnaround [ˈtɜːnəraʊnd]n. (车辆)回转场，回车道；周转时 间；(经济形势等)突然好转
[05:11.76]interim [ˈɪntərɪm]a. 暂时的，临时的；中间的 n. 间歇， 过渡时期 例 He submitted an interim report to his boss. 搭 in the interim 在过渡期间
[05:23.04]token [ˈtəʊkən]n. 专用辅币；代金券；象征；记号；纪 念品 a. 象征的
[05:27.72]prevention [prɪˈvenʃn]n. 预防；防止 例 It is well known that prevention is better than a cure.
[05:36.60]sanitary [ˈsænətri]a. 有益于健康的；卫生的，公共卫生 的；消过毒的 n. 公共厕所
[05:42.24]coach [kəʊtʃ]v. 训练，辅导 n. 教练；客车车厢 例 The venture capital firms with consistent interests and behaviour can coach entrepreneurs to grow the business and increase shareholder value. 搭 coaching grid 训练场地 / coach route 长途 公共汽车路线 / drive a coach and horse through 使无用；使失效
[06:08.88]coincide [ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd]vi. 同时发生；相符，相一致；位置 重合，重叠 例 The journalist's interest in a scoop and the source's self-interest coincide. 搭 coincide with 巧合；同时发生
[06:24.60]shift [ʃɪft]n. 轮班；转换；移动，变化；手段
[06:27.84]temporary [ˈtemprəri]a. 暂时的，临时的；短暂的 n. 临时 工，临时雇员
[06:33.00]primary [ˈpraɪməri]a. 首要的，主要的；初级的；基本 的；第一手的 搭 primary health care 初级保健护理 / primary responsibility 首要责任
[06:43.80]repatriation [ˌriːˌpætriˈeɪʃn]n. 遣送回国；归国；汇回本国
[06:48.96]brochure [ˈbrəʊʃə(r)]n. (宣传产品的)小册子 例 We will send you a brochure on the various kinds of bicycles now available for export.
[07:01.44]countervailing [ˈkaʊntəveɪlɪŋ]adj. 补偿的，弥补的；抵消的
[07:06.72]showroom [ˈʃəʊruːm]n. 展厅；陈列室；样品间
[07:10.32]competitive [kəmˈpetətɪv]a. 比赛的；竞争的
[07:14.28]blanket [ˈblæŋkɪt]a. 总括的；综合的 vt. 使包括进去 例 The reporter reported the blanket coverage of the air pollution in Beijing. 搭 be blanketed into/in 被纳入；被包括进去
[07:29.52]presumably [prɪˈzjuːməbli]ad. 据推测；大概，可能 例 Presumably the boss has made the decision of firing him.
[07:39.72]excursion [ɪkˈskɜːʃn]n. 远足，短途旅行；游览团体 a. 远足 的，旅行的 例 The team leader arranged an excursion to the seaside for the whole team. 搭 make an excursion to...去…旅游
[07:55.20]condemn [kənˈdem]v. 依法没收或征用(财产等)；谴责，指 责；判刑，宣告有罪 例 If they think someone is lying to them, they will feel angry and condemn him. 搭 condemn sb. for sth. 因某事谴责某人 / condemn sb. to death 判某人死刑
[08:13.92]uncontrollable [ˌʌnkənˈtrəʊləbl]a. 不可控制的；无法管束的
[08:19.20]co-worker [ˈkəʊwɜːkə(r)]n. 合作者；同事 例 Before you leave the office, you should have the contact information of every co- worker you plan to stay in touch with.
[08:34.92]quandary [ˈkwɒndəri]n. 困惑；窘境；左右两难 搭 be in a quandary about 对…左右为难
[08:41.64]franchise [ˈfræntʃaɪz]vt. 赋予特权 n. 特许经营权，特许总 代理权；公民权，选举权 例 Windows is one of the franchise brands and products of Microsoft.
[08:54.36]unchangeable [ʌnˈtʃeɪndʒəbl]a. 不变的；不能改变的；安定的 例 The company has already developed its own business model that is unchangeable.
[09:07.56]registered [ˈredʒɪstə(r)d]a. 已注册的；已登记的；记名的
[09:12.36]irritate [ˈɪrɪteɪt]vt. 使恼怒，使烦躁；使(身体)不适，使疼 痛；刺激 vi. 引起不快 例 No one can irritate her except for her son.
[09:22.68]attest [əˈtest]v. 证明，证实；表明 例 The government investigators required the company's accountants to attest to the accuracy of their reports.
[09:36.84]predicament [prɪˈdɪkəmənt]n. 困境，窘境；处境
[09:41.04]caretaker [ˈkeəteɪkə(r)]n. 值班人员；看管人 a. 临时代理的 例 He signed a six-month contract to serve as the caretaker of an amusement park. 搭 caretaker government 临时政府 / caretaker president 临时总统
[09:59.40]contemporary [kənˈtemprəri]a. 现代的，当代的；同时代的 n. 当代人，现代人；同时代的人 例 Their impact on contemporary society is enormous and unprecedented. 搭 be contemporary with 与…同时代的 / contemporary literature 现代文学
[10:19.44]saturate [ˈsætʃəreɪt]vt. 浸透；使充满；使饱和 a. 浸透 的；饱和的 例 The manager is saturated with business knowledge. 搭 be saturated with 浸透；充满 / saturate oneself in 埋头于…中
[10:35.04]constraint [kənˈstreɪnt]n. 强制，强迫；限制，约束；紧张 感 例 There have been several attempts to deal with this kind of constraint.
[10:47.04]territory [ˈterətri]n. 领土，版图；领域，区域，范围 搭 guard one's territory 保护某人的领域
[10:54.48]warehouse [ˈweəhaʊs]n. 仓库，货栈；大商店 vt. 贮入仓 库；以他人名义购进股票
[11:00.12]wording [ˈwɜːdɪŋ]n. 措辞；用语 搭 relevant wording 得当的措辞
[11:05.40]drain [dreɪn]vt. 使耗尽 vi. 慢慢地枯竭 n. (财富等的)不 断外流；(时间、金钱的)消耗 例 The drain of money from this country is a serious problem.
[11:17.16]boost [buːst]vt. 增强，使增长；提高；促进；激励 n. 增长；促进 例 In China, the easier and cheaper on-line payment service is boosting the industry of e- commerce. 搭 boost sb. up 支援某人，帮助某人
[11:33.96]active [ˈæktɪv]a. 活跃的，流通的；现行的 例 China has been playing an active role in the peace and stability of the whole world.
[11:45.60]dilute [daɪˈluːt; daɪˈljuːt]vt. 稀释，冲淡 a. 稀释的，冲 淡的 例 The government has taken some measures to dilute public fears about food safety.
[11:59.04]theocracy [θiˈɒkrəsi]n. 神权政治 搭 formation and development of theocracy 神 权政治的形成与发展
[12:07.56]surcharge [ˈsɜːtʃɑːdʒ]n. 额外费；附加罚款 搭 surcharge on... …的附加费 sales volume 销售量；销售额
[12:15.84]metropolitan [ˌmetrəˈpɒlɪtən]a. 大都会的；主要都市的；大城 市的 搭 metropolitan area network 城域网
[12:24.48]predatory [ˈpredətri]a. 掠夺的；以掠夺为目的的；损人利 己的
[12:29.16]restitution [ˌrestɪˈtjuːʃn]n. 恢复；归还；赔偿 搭 make a restitution of sth. to sb. 向某人归还 (或赔偿)某物
[12:38.28]anniversary [ˌænɪˈvɜːsəri]n. 周年纪念；周年纪念日 例 If there is a lesson to be drawn on this anniversary, it is that the United States is one nation and one people united by common ideals. 搭 anniversary issue 周年纪念特刊，纪念专号 / wedding anniversary 结婚周年纪念日
[13:02.52]contingency [kənˈtɪndʒənsi]n. 突发事件，意外事故；偶然性 例 Establishing contingency reserve is an example of risk acceptance strategy.
[13:15.48]ingenious [ɪnˈdʒiːniəs]a. 灵巧的；有独创性的；设计独特 的；制作精巧的 例 He is an ingenious person who can make remarkable sculptures from the most ordinary materials.
[13:30.60]glamour [ˈɡlæmə(r)]n. 魅力，诱惑力；刺激，冒险；[pl.] 热门股票 vt. 迷住；美化 例 The quick increase of sales volume confirms the glamour of the BMW brand.
[13:44.04]cut [kʌt]n. 削减，降低 v. 减少，削减 a. 减少的，削 减的 例 When they got people to sign up, you would get a cut of the profits as well. 搭 cut back 减少
[13:56.28]compliance [kəmˈplaɪəns]n. 遵从，执行；达到(标准)；顺从 例 Our bank is facing much higher charges for compliance with the new legislation on the financial services industry. 搭 in compliance with 依从，遵照
[14:15.48]transit [ˈtrænzɪt]n. 通过；过境，中转；运输 vt. 通过； 转运 vi. 通过 搭 in transit 在运输途中
[14:22.44]branch [brɑːntʃ]n. (公司的)分支，分店，分部；(政府的) 分支机构 vi. 分叉；分支；派生，衍生 例 They have decided to close that branch down. 搭 branch off 岔开；分叉 / branch out 扩大活 动范围；扩充(业务等)
[14:38.16]comply [kəmˈplaɪ]v. 遵从，依从；服从 例 Even if they do comply, it would introduce an element of risk that could affect the bankability of their project.
[14:52.68]multilingual [ˌmʌltiˈlɪŋɡwəl]a. 使用多种语言的 搭 multilingual dictionary 多语词典 / multilingual information processing 多文种信息 处理 / multilingual publication 多语种出版物
[15:08.88]viand [ˈvaɪənd]n. 各种食品(尤指美味菜肴)
[15:12.24]refurbish [ˌriːˈfɜːbɪʃ]vt. 刷新；再磨光；整修 例 This mobi le phone must have been refurbished by someone.
[15:22.20]poll [pəʊl]n. 民意测验，民意调查 搭 carry out a poll 进行民意测验
